    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Bones are your body's frame! Without them, you would be floppy, like a jelly.",
      "punch": "floppy",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦴",
        "text": "Bones hold you up",
        "cue": "frame",
        "sub": "No more floppy!",
        "sub_cue": "floppy"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else do bones do?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They protect the soft parts inside. Your skull guards your brain, and your ribs guard your heart and lungs.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Bone guards",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🧠",
            "label": "Skull: brain",
            "cue": "skull"
          },
          {
            "icon": "❤️",
            "label": "Ribs: heart",
            "cue": "ribs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🫁",
            "label": "Ribs: lungs",
            "cue": "lungs"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do bones help me move, too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Muscles pull on your bones to move them, and joints like your knees and elbows let you bend.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Let's move",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "💪",
            "label": "Muscles pull",
            "cue": "muscles"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦵",
            "label": "Knees bend",
            "cue": "knees"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🤸",
            "label": "Elbows bend",
            "cue": "elbows"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How many bones do I have?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Grown-ups have 206 bones. Babies are born with more, about 300, and some of them join together as they grow!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👶",
        "text": "Babies: about 300",
        "cue": "babies",
        "sub": "Grown-ups: 206",
        "sub_cue": "grown"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Whoa! Are bones alive?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They are! Bones are living and growing. And inside many bones is soft marrow that makes new blood cells.",
      "punch": "living",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔴",
        "text": "Marrow makes blood cells",
        "cue": "marrow",
        "sub": "Bones are alive!",
        "sub_cue": "living"
      }
    },
